>   You must get the size of the executable below 540k.

Actually, I have found the 540 K limit to be a bit conservative.  I have
defined WIZARD, EXPLORE_MODE, THEOLOGY, ALTARS, STRONGHOLD, DGK, MSDOSCOLOR,
MEDUSA and EXP_ON_BOTL, producing a 571,426 byte .EXE file which runs fine.  I
have 640 K RAM, no extended/expanded memory, am running MSDOS 3.3, and
admittedly must have NO TSR's loaded, but it runs.  No, I don't have an
overlay linker in the code, but I have been trying to use LINKOVL.OBJ 3.01 to
increase further the options I can include.  (So far it only generates fixup
overflow and unresolved external errors. :-( )

There do, however, seem to be certain combinations of options that don't work.
For example, if you define ALTARS and THEOLOGY, but neither HARD nor SOUNDS,
then LINK will detect bribe() as an undefined symbol in priest.c.  (The fix is
in demon.c.  Change the #if defined(... so that bribe gets compiled if ALTARS
is defined, i.e. remove the "&& defined(SOUNDS)".)


